G1611.def:
ἔκ-στασις, -εως, ἡ
(ἐξίστημι) [in LXX: Genèse 27:33, 1 Rois 14:15, Eze.26:16, al. (חֲרָדָה); 2 Chroniques 14:14 17:10 20:29 (פַּחַד), al. ;] 
__1. a displacement (Arist.). 
__2. An abnormal condition of the mind, in which the subject passes out of his usual self-control (Hippocr.); in NT (Kennedy, Sources, 121 f.); 
__(a) a trance: Actes 10:10 11:5 22:17; 
__(b) amazement: Marc 5:42 16:8, Luc 5:26, Actes 3:19.†

G1623.def:
ἐκτός, 
adv. [in LXX Juges 8:26 20:15, 3Ki.10:13, al. (בַּד, Juges 5:28 (בַּד), בַּד), Cantique des cantiques 4:1-3 (בַּד), al, ;] 
__1. as adv., outside, beyond: τὸ ἐ., with poss. genitive, the outside, Matthieu 23:26; in late Gk. (see Deiss., BS, 118), pleonastic, ἐκτός εἰ μή, 1 Corinthiens 14:5 15:2, 1 Timothée 5:19. 
__2. With force of prep., with genitive; 
__(a) outside of: 1 Corinthiens 6:18, 2 Corinthiens 12:2; 
__(b) beyond, besides, except: Actes 26:22, 1 Corinthiens 15:27.†

G1627.def:
ἐκ-φέρω 
[in LXX chiefly for יָצָא hi. ;] 
__1. to carry out, bring out: with accusative of thing(s), Luc 15:22, 1 Timothée 6:7; with accusative of person(s), Marc 8:23, Actes 5:15; of the dead for burial (cf. κομίζω), Actes 5:6, 9-10. 
__2. to bring forth; 
__(a) of women (Hipp., Arist., al.); 
__(b) of the ground (Hdt.): Hébreux 6:8.†

G1658.def:
ἐλεύθερος, -α, -ον 
[in LXX chiefly for חׇפְשִׁי ;] 
free; 
__(a) in civil sense, not a slave: Jean 8:33, 1 Corinthiens 7:21-22 12:13, Galates 3:28, Éphésiens 6:8, Colossiens 3:11, Apocalypse 6:15 13:16 19:18; fem., Galates 4:22-23, 30; 
__(b) as regards restraint and obligation in general: Matthieu 17:26, 1 Corinthiens 9:1; before ἐκ, 1 Corinthiens 9:19; ἀπό, Romains 7:3; with inf., 1 Corinthiens 7:39; from the law, Galates 4:26, 1 Pierre 2:16; from sin, Jean 8:32, 36; τῇ δικαιοσύνῃ, as regards righteousness, Romains 6:20 (Cremer, 249).†
